  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Capacity Building to Promote Participation in Trade of Small and Medium Enterprises</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Regional Capacity Building to Promote Participation in Trade of Small and Medium Enterprises  The Grant would play a key role in developing programs to support the participation of small and medium enterprises (SMEs) in international trade opportunities in Costa Rica, Guatemala, El Salvador, Honduras and Nicaragua (Central America) by financing training, services, and the establishment of SME business service centers. Specifically, the Grant would finance the following activities: a) train government officials and partner organizations on how to establish and administer the trade-related SMEs support programs, including business centers; b) promote the programs among potential SME clients, and (c) support the implementation of the pilot programs work plan during their first year of operation.</narrative>
  </description>
